      "comment": "SEASIDE BOULEVARD (6) is a smart filly who comes through the Breeders Challenge series where she was second in a heat two back at Menangle. She showed her class when runner-up in the Queensland Oaks over the winter and should be at peak fitness now. Won her lone attempt at this distance and looks well placed. CORTEZ (1) hasn't featured in two starts off a spell but has had tougher barriers, the latest when off the back line. Has won when third-up before and is much better served by the ace draw. TUKAHA (8) draws wide but was good in his last-start placing and has won a trial since. KOBES CHAINSAW (9) resumes after 11 months having come through his maiden campaign with a 50 per cent strike rate. Readied with two trials. May be worth including.",
